    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2103_03330_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "small portion of GPU resources for the zero-copy accesses and leaves the rest for computationally intense workloads. Finally, we build an end-to-end zero-copy GCN training flow in PyTorch. To enable zero-copy memory access, we devise a new class of tensor called \"unified tensor\". This tensor provides an address mapping of host memory for GPUs so they can directly access host 2 memory with zero-copy accesses. By simply declaring multiple unified tensor instances for multiple GPUs, our GCN trainin" .

