    kg:textSpan "With more misaligned accesses, the efficiency of the nave zero-copy implementation drops to 78-82% while the optimized zero-copy implementation can achieve 88-93% of efficiency. In general, the results re-emphasize the importance of making cacheline-aligned accesses whenever using zero-copy accesses. For savvy programmers, we expect them to understand the underlying hardware mechanism and to consider padding the input data if the overhead is not too big. However, even if they fail to do so, our " .

