    kg:docId "2105.10554_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2105_10554_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "for a general GNN, or the summed numerator and softmax denominator for a GAT) are written to the output buffer after each edge computation. For a GAT, the values of exp( e ik ) are also added over the neighborhood to create the denominator for the softmax. Finally, the accumulation over neighbors is divided by the denominator, in the SFU to obtain the result. When all components of the sum for vertex i are accumulated, the result is sent through the Activation unit and written to DRAM. VI. G RAP" .

