    kg:textSpan "GAS enables constant inference time complexity: The time complexity of model inference is reduced to a then the output error is bounded by to be able to reason about structural differences across neighborhoods directly during training. We now show that GNNs that scale by sampling edges are not capable of doing so: h ( ) v h ( ) v k 2 + ( + ) k 1 k 2 |N ( v ) | . Proposition 3. Let f ( L ) : V R d be a L -layered GNN as expressive as the WL test in distinguishing the L -hop neighborhood around ea" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2106_05609_rag__chunk_010> a kg:Chunk ;
