    kg:textSpan "entire neighborhood of all nodes in the previous layer and compute the sampling probability for all candidate nodes in the next layer. Thus, this sampling method has significantly higher computation overhead. Furthermore, when applying this method on a large graph, it still constructs a mini-batch with many isolated nodes, especially for nodes in the first layer (Table 5). LazyGCN. Even though layer-wise sampling methods effectively address the neighborhood explosion issue, they failed to invest" .

