    kg:textSpan "is provided in Appendix A. 3.5 Theoretical Analysis In this section, we establish the convergence rate of GNS which is inspired by the work of Ramezani et al. [ 11 ]. It shows that under mild assumption, GNS enjoys comparable convergence rate as underlying node-wise sampling in training. Here, the convergence rate of GNS mainly depends on the graph degree and the size of cached set. We focus on a two-layer GCN for simplicity and denote the loss functions of full-batch, mini-batch and proposed GN" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2106_06150_rag__chunk_012> a kg:Chunk ;
