    kg:textSpan "propagation of messages between neighbors in the graph is only done once in a non-learnable manner during pre-processing. The use of non-learnable messages, however, limits the expressiveness Graph neural networks (GNNs), also called message passing networks ( Gilmer et al. , 2017 ; Kipf & Welling , 2017 ; Scarselli et al. , 2008 ), are widely applied in various types of graph-related problems ( Shi et al. , 2020 ; Corso et al. , 2020 ; Li et al. , 2019 ; Zhang & Chen , 2018 ). At every layer in" .

