    kg:textSpan "edge connection density of each subgraph. In general, the more number of the subgraphs/partitions would lead to denser edges connections within each subgraph, which may bring better computation and memory locality. Second , the processing granularity is controlled by the batch size. This would determine the size of graphs that will be fit into the GPU at each round of execution. The selection of batch size would maximize the utilization of the GPU while respecting the GPU computation and memory " .

