    kg:textSpan "that if there is little difference between the output distribution of one algorithm A and the uniform distribution, A will not inuence the convergence rate. [ 39 ] denes the difference , named shufing error , as the total variation distance between the two distributions, and proves that, if bM / n , the convergence 6 graphs. To this end, we propose a novel graph partition algorithm. We make two key innovations: rst, we adopt a multilevel coarsening strategy to greatly reduce the complexity of pa" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2112_08541_rag__chunk_012> a kg:Chunk ;
