    kg:textSpan "PyG [ 34 ] and DGL [ 131 ]. 5.1 GPU Kernel Acceleration [TABLE id=2306.14052_p22_t3] caption: GPUs are powerful hardware accelerators that can greatly speed up computations required in DNN training and inference. Under this context, GPU kernels refer to specialized programs optimized to be executed in parallel on the many processing units of a GPU, enabling DNN computations to be much faster and more efficient. Although GPUs are popular in being used for DL acceleration, accelerating GNNs with G" .

