    kg:textSpan "be received for each partition). To mitigate the issues caused by boundary nodes, BNS-GCN simply adopts Boundary Node Sampling, achieving drastically saved communication, reduced memory, and balanced computation, while maintaining full-graph accuracy. The sampling rate can be as low as 0.1 as suggested by the authors. SAR [ 94 ] also discovers the exploded memory issue in partition parallelism and proposes Sequential Aggregation and Rematerialization scheme. Specifically, each worker receives de" .

