    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/p1937-peng_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "a single point of failure. Also, it should be noted that only NeuGraph and Roc support full-GNN processing, while all others need sampling. More recently, DGCL [ 3 ], a communication library for distributed full-GNN training, tries to reduce the communication by nding optimal communication routes in specic system topology for every node in the entire graph. Regardless of the substantial overhead caused by planning communication for each node before every execution, it still follows the conventio" .

