    kg:textSpan "2 middle row. Like graph coarsening, graph sparsification has been studied and widely used before GNNs became popular [ 6 , 111 , 118 , 119 ]. Graph sparsification methods usually try to find a sparsified G that can well approximate the properties of the original G . That is keeping all the nodes in G and removing less-important edges without disconnecting G . Example properties preserved by existing graph sparsification methods include the total weight of cuts [ 6 ], spectral properties [ 118 ," .

