    kg:textSpan "is naturally fit for existing GPU interconnects optimized for throughput and has been optimized by many libraries (e.g., NCCL). In contrast, distributed full-graph GNN (with the entire graph cached on GPUs) is much more challenging since it requires sparse irregular communication that is naturally at odds with the existing hardware interconnects, and fewer efforts have optimized its performance. Second , the GNN pipeline workload is more irregular and non-structural and can easily cause pipeline" .

