    kg:textSpan "advantages: Latency friendly: When working on either of the two phases, all the hardware components will be instantiated and subsequently reused for the other phase, thus reducing the startup latency of GNN inference which would otherwise be much higher if a pipeline structure was employed for the two phases as in [5]. B. G-CoS: the co-optimization formulation Utilization friendly: Given the workload allocation scheme as introduced later in Sec. IV-C, all subaccelerators work on different parts " .

