    kg:textSpan "graph, after which the global state is aggregated into an estimate. D). Power Graph Neural Networks (PGNN) [3]: The PGNN incorporates a multi-hop convolution and is often used as a component in a more complex Line Graph Neural Network model. Our selection of benchmarks provides adequate diversity across several dimensions in a GNN algorithm: spatial versus spectral convolution, different aggregation schemes, large vs small models, and different types of graph traversal. GNN Accelerator Model: We" .

