    kg:textSpan "set of processes to sample mini-batches independently and send them back to the trainer process for mini-batch computation. The construction of subgraphs S for multiple caches C can be parallelized. = deg ( )/ V deg ( ) . (6) For a power-law graph, we only need to maintain a small cache of nodes to cover majority of the nodes in the graph. If the training set only accounts for a small portion of the nodes in the graph, we use short random walks to compute the sampling probability. Define N ( ) a" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2106_06150_rag__chunk_014> a kg:Chunk ;
