    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2109_08983_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "G-CoS: GNN-Accelerator Co-Search Towards Both Better Accuracy and Efciency Yongan Zhang 1 , Haoran You 1 , Yonggan Fu 1 , Tong Geng 2 , Ang Li 2 , Yingyan Lin 1 1 Rice University, Houston, TX; 2 Pacic Northwest National Laboratory, Richland, WA Corresponding to: 1 yingyan.lin@rice.edu To tackle GNNs prohibitive inference cost, various ef- cient GNN inference techniques have been developed. On the algorithm level, several pioneering GNN compression techniques have been developed. For instance, tw" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2109_08983_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2109.08983_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "2109.08983_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2109_08983_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "solutions, their achievable efciency is still not sufcient for enabling extensive GNN inference applications due to GNNs extremely dynamic and irregular data accesses and thus excessive acceleration cost. Motivated by the great success of algorithm-accelerator co-exploration works for CNN accelerations [15][21], this work targets to co-optimize both the GNN structures and their accelerators with boosted development speed, and makes the following contributions: Graph neural networks (GNNs) [1] ha" .

