    kg:textSpan "could be small (e.g., 1000), the computation graph samples could be exponentially larger due to the k -hop neighborhood and the associated features. A major reason for such large size is not the graph structure in itself, but the features, whose sizes typically range in 100s to several 1000s [ 29 , 41 , 66 , 68 ]. In real world graphs consisting of billions of nodes and edges [ 15 , 55 ], the 2-hop neighborhoods could be up to an order of magnitude larger than the 1-hop neighborhood [ 43 ]. When" .

