    kg:textSpan "which we describe in detail in this section. [TABLE id=osdi21-gandhi_p5_t1] caption: Table 1: Partitioning techniques are not effective in GNNs. All schemes, except hash, reduce the epoch time, but at the cost of signicant partitioning time or memory overheads. columns: scheme | time_s | memory_gb | epoch_s row: scheme=Hash [ 48 ]; time_s=2.87; memory_gb=58; epoch_s=9.833 row: scheme=METIS [ 38 ]; time_s=4264; memory_gb=63; epoch_s=5.295 row: scheme=RandomVertexCut [ 22 ]; time_s=36.95; memory_g" .

