    kg:textSpan "second type is aggregation with special edge features ( e.g. , weights, and edge vectors that are computed by combining source and target nodes) applied to each neighbor node, as in Graph Isomorphism Network (GIN) [ 55 ]. This type of GNN must work on large full-dimensional node embeddings to compute the special edge features at the node aggregation. In this case, the fast memory ( e.g. , shared memory of GPU Stream-Multiprocessors) is not large enough to exploit memory locality. However, improv" .

