    kg:textSpan "Table 4). Moreover, we show that singleGPU training can be sufficient for large-scale graphs: We use MariusGNN to train a GNN over the entire hyperlink graph from the Common Crawl 2012 web corpus, a graph with 3.5B nodes (web pages) and 128B edges (hyperlinks between pages) (Table 1) . MariusGNN can learn vector representations for all 3.5B nodes using only a single machine with one GPU, 60GB of RAM, and a large SSD, leading to a cost of just $564/epoch . Achieving these results required innovat" .

