    kg:textSpan "partitions are connected by edges, dropping these cross-partition edges results in information loss about the graph structure. To avoid this information loss, distributed GNN training methods require frequent communication between GPUs. For example, prior approaches support the cross-partition connectivity by synchronizing node embeddings between partitions [34, 23, 24]. Preprint. Under review. Degree-Aware Reweighting Loss Weight Communication-Free Distributed Computing Partition 1 1 !! !! 1 2 " .

