    kg:textSpan "the maximum amount of available GPU memory for the 2.2 Data Parallel Training and Partition The current design of GNN systems such as DGL, balance computation across multiple GPUs but make them share a single copy of graph data ( DGL Team , 2019 ). When directly applying the above GNN-aware caching method to this setting, we observe a cache inefciency phenomena, i.e., the cache hit ratio keeps decreasing with the increasing number of GPUs. This is because the single graph serves the data visitin" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2106_05609_rag__chunk_015> a kg:Chunk ;
