    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2106_05609_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "is quickly mitigated by faster training times: Computing the partitioning of a graph with 2M nodes takes only about 2050 seconds (depending on the number of clusters). 6.2. GAS is fast and memory-efcient For training large-scale GNNs, GPU memory consumption will directly dictate the scalability of the given approach. Here, we show how GAS maintains a low GPU memory footprint while, in contrast to other scalability approaches, accounts for all available information inside a GNNs receptive eld in " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2107_08709_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
